# Spotify Developer app client ID (from https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard).
# This project uses PKCE, not the client-credentials flow, so no client secret is
# ever needed — see .claude/SECURITY.md.
#
# Register these two redirect URIs in the dashboard:
#   http://127.0.0.1:5178/callback                       (the host's own login)
#   https://vdwolde.github.io/Song-Snitch/callback.html   (a player's own login, top-tracks mode only)
# The second one is github-pages/callback.html in this repo — published automatically
# by .github/workflows/pages.yml, nothing to upload by hand. See
# .claude/DECISIONS.md ADR-006 for why there are two instead of one.
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=cf927e357a0b4485b77310b99e3fb3a2

# PORT / BIND_LAN / UI_ORIGIN are NOT read from this file — Start Song Snitch.bat and
# `npm run dev` already set them as real shell environment variables, which is required:
# they're read at module-import time, before a .env file would be loaded.
